# Git Push — Development Branch Only

## Trigger phrases

Activate this workflow when the user says: **push**, **commit and push**, **publish to GitHub**, **ship to development**, **sync up**, or similar.

Pair with **Git-Pull-Sync-Rule** when they ask to sync both directions.

---

## Policy

- **Never push directly to `main`.** All agent pushes go to **`development`**.
- **`main` is merge-only** — the user reviews and merges `development` → `main` on GitHub after approval.
- **Only push documented work** — undocumented code changes are not ready to push.

**Remote:** `origin` → `https://github.com/WillMoose23/vibecoded-pokemon-engine.git`

---

## Pre-push gate (all must pass)

1. **Documentation** (Documentation-Rule): `/docs/source_doc.md` and/or `/docs/tools_doc.md` updated for changed code.
2. **Tracker** (Logging-Rule): `/docs/tracker.md` entries exist; `STATUS` is accurate (e.g. `REVIEW` or `DONE`).
3. **Tests:**
   ```bash
   make test
   python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -q
   ```
4. **Cursor plans** — sync global plans into the repo before push:
   ```bash
   python3 tools/sync_cursor_plans.py
   ```
   Commit any new/changed files under `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`.
5. **No secrets** — never stage `.env`, tokens, or ignored caches (see `.gitignore`).

If any gate fails, fix or report blockers; **do not push**.

---

## Branch workflow

```bash
cd /Users/rheyn/Desktop/project
git fetch origin
git checkout development
git pull origin development --no-rebase
```

- Never commit on `main` — checkout `development` first.
- If `origin/development` is missing, create with `git push -u origin development` (one-time).

---

## Commit and push

Run in parallel: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log -3 --oneline`

Then:

```bash
git add <relevant files>
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
<Why, 1-2 sentences>

Tracker: <ID if applicable>
EOF
)"
git push -u origin development
git status
```

---

## After push

Report:

1. Pushed branch: **`development`**
2. Compare URL: `https://github.com/WillMoose23/vibecoded-pokemon-engine/compare/main...development`
3. User merges to **`main`** when approved — agent does not merge unless explicitly asked.

---

## Forbidden without explicit user override

- `git push origin main`
- `git push --force` to `main` or `development`
- Push with failing tests or missing docs/tracker updates
